course: dictionary
lesson: 10705
title: Not right for the job
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unsuitable means not right, or not fitting, for a purpose, a person or a situation. Look at the words around it to work it out. «Children do not need diets unless a doctor says so; bots may give unsuitable food and body advice.» The sentence is about children, so unsuitable food and advice must be food and advice that are not right for them.
explain: Ask yourself what would fit here, then swap in your own meaning. «Safety settings and children's accounts filter unsuitable content» means the settings block content that is not right for children. If "not right for children" still makes sense in the sentence, you have understood it.
explain: Unsuitable is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as food, content, clothes or shoes. Look for the phrases unsuitable for and unsuitable clothes, because they show you what it is describing and why it does not fit.
fact: Unsuitable means not right or not appropriate for a purpose, person or situation.
fact: Suitable means right or fitting. The un- at the start turns it into the opposite.
fact: Unsuitable clothes or shoes can be dangerous, for example flip-flops on a climbing wall.
fact: Films and games may be unsuitable for children, so check the age rating before you watch or play.
fact: Phrases to remember: unsuitable for, as in «unsuitable for a snowy hill», and unsuitable clothes.
exercise: «Children do not need diets unless a doctor says so; bots may give unsuitable food and body advice.» What does unsuitable mean here? | Very cheap to buy | *Not right for children | Brand new and expensive | Tasty and healthy
exercise: Flip-flops are ___ footwear for a climbing wall. Which word fits best? | luminous | *unsuitable | ancient | famished
exercise: «Safety settings filter unsuitable content, but they are not perfect, so telling a grown-up still matters.» Why does the author say telling a grown-up still matters? | Because content is always suitable for children | Because grown-ups always know everything about every website | *Because filters can miss content that is not right for children | Because the settings are perfect and need no help
test: Which word means the opposite of suitable? | ancient | *unsuitable | happy | barely
test: Which sentence uses unsuitable correctly? | Thin sandals are unsuitable, so the mountain is warm and sunny | The sandals were unsuitable, so they were very ancient | Unsuitable the walk was sandals snowy | *Thin sandals are unsuitable for a snowy mountain walk
exam: Mum says the film is unsuitable for your age. What does she mean? | It is the best film she has ever seen | *It is not right for your age | It is in a language you do not know | It is too short to watch
